        "id": 139611,
        "name": "bluedarky",
        "username": "bluedarky",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluedarky/{size}/1975_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-21T18:35:28.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It has already been an official ruling that more than 1 Overdrive played would still only result in 2 Strikes max. The reason Pydro gave above is 100% correct.Maybe this is like Crowbars where there has been a change in the previous official ruling. But I'm inclined to think it's a bug.Hey MigrantP, are you lurking around anywhere?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It's a bug, it's mentioned at the bottom of the Fireside chat thread.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Even if Mr. Fixer is able to play multiple Overdrives in one turn, he still only gets to use Strike twice that turn.</p>\n</blockquote>",
