      {
        "id": 139614,
        "name": "bluedarky",
        "username": "bluedarky",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluedarky/{size}/1975_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-22T17:22:03.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"gailon24\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/gailon24/48/2177_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> gailon24:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Awesome, will do. &nbsp;Wanted to verify what was SUPPOSED to happen first. &nbsp;Honestly I didn't even know that if overdrive is played on someone ELSE'S turn that I would get ANY strikes.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You always follow the cards instructions to the letter.</p>\n<p>But for a little more clarification, extra powers work as follows.</p>\n<p>If you gain an extra power on your turn, you use it during your power phase.</p>\n<p>If you gain an extra power on someone elses turn, you use it immediately.</p>",
